  "name": "Example: Evaluating a Definite Integral Using the Constant Multiple Rule",
  "problem": "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int_{-1}^{2} 9 x^2 \\, \\textrm d x .$",
  "worked_solution": "Factoring the constant out of the integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}9{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =9{\\int }_{-1}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =9\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}\\,{|}_{-1}^{2} \\\\  & =3{x}^{3}\\,{|}_{-1}^{2} \\\\  & =3({2}^{3}-(-1)^{3}) \\\\  & =3(8-(-1)) \\\\  & =3\\cdot 9 \\\\  & =27.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
